---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { projects } from '../../data/projects';

const dextra = projects[0];
const shot = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/screenshots/dextra.webp`;
const home = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/#work`;
---

<Layout
  title="DEXTRA case study · Faras Fadhil Firdaus"
  description="How the DEXTRA interactive prototype handles governed AI operations: request, plan, approval, mandate, execution, and audit."
  canonical={new URL('case-study/dextra', Astro.site ?? 'https://frzz969.github.io').href}
>
  <article class="section section--case">
    <div class="container case">
      <header class="case__head">
        <a class="case__back mono" href={home}>← Back to selected work</a>
        <span class="case__index mono" aria-hidden="true">03 / Selected Work</span>
        <span class="case__eyebrow eyebrow">Case study · interactive prototype · 2026</span>
        <h1 class="case__title">{dextra.title}</h1>
        <p class="case__subtitle">Governed Enterprise AI Workforce &amp; Operations Platform</p>
        <p class="case__lead lead">
          An interactive prototype for exploring AI-assisted operations. AI reads, analyzes and
          recommends. Writing to data or the outside world needs an approved plan, a human mandate,
          and an audit record.
        </p>
        <div class="case__strip">
          <span>Status · interactive prototype, not production enterprise software</span>
          <a class="case__strip-link" href={dextra.liveUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Live demo ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="case__section" aria-labelledby="case-problem">
        <span class="case__number num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div class="case__content">
          <h2 id="case-problem" class="case__h2 h3">The Problem</h2>
          <p class="body">
            Operational work is spread across tools. Tasks, questions and actions arrive without a
            clear record of who authorized them or what was actually executed. An AI assistant that
            can write to systems makes that gap more serious, not less.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case__section" aria-labelledby="case-approach">
        <span class="case__number num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div class="case__content">
          <h2 id="case-approach" class="case__h2 h3">The Approach</h2>
          <p class="body">
            Split reading from writing. Four specialist AI workers, covering Finance, HR, Inventory
            and Operations, analyze context and propose a plan. A deterministic Policy Validator
            checks that plan against policy. Only a human approval and an explicit mandate allow an
            action to change data or the outside world.
          </p>
          <p class="body case__small">
            The Policy Validator is a governance engine, not an AI agent. The prototype is a place to
            examine that boundary; it is not a production deployment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case__section" aria-labelledby="case-architecture">
        <span class="case__number num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div class="case__content">
          <h2 id="case-architecture" class="case__h2 h3">Architecture</h2>
          <p class="body">
            The same six-step path shown in the selected-work section, described here as a flow:
          </p>
          <ol class="case__flow">
            <li><span class="mono">Request</span> A task or operational action enters the platform.</li>
            <li><span class="mono">Plan</span> Specialized workers read context and propose a plan.</li>
            <li><span class="mono">Approval</span> A human reviews the proposal; the Policy Validator checks it against policy.</li>
            <li><span class="mono">Mandate</span> A human authorizes the specific action to run.</li>
            <li><span class="mono">Execution</span> Only after approval and mandate may data or an outside system change.</li>
            <li><span class="mono">Audit</span> The request, approval, run and mandate are recorded.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case__section" aria-labelledby="case-implementation">
        <span class="case__number num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
        <div class="case__content">
          <h2 id="case-implementation" class="case__h2 h3">Implementation</h2>
          <p class="body">
            Built as an interactive prototype with Next.js and React on the front end, Python and
            FastAPI behind it, and MCP for integration. The governance path adds a deterministic
            policy validator and an audit trail.
          </p>
          <p class="body case__small">
            Prototype limits: this is a working demonstration of the approval model, not a hardened
            enterprise rollout. No production customer, deployment guarantee or accuracy figure is
            claimed here.
          </p>
          <ul class="case__tags">
            {dextra.focus.map((tag) => <li class="case__tag">{tag}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case__section" aria-labelledby="case-evidence">
        <span class="case__number num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
        <div class="case__content">
          <h2 id="case-evidence" class="case__h2 h3">Evidence</h2>
          <figure class="case__figure">
            <div class="case__frame">
              <img
                src={shot}
                width="1440"
                height="900"
                loading="lazy"
                alt="Screenshot dashboard DEXTRA asli: Executive Operations Overview dengan metrik workforce, approval queue, dan human authorization."
              />
            </div>
            <figcaption class="meta-label">
              Captured from the live dashboard at dextra-office-agent.vercel.app/overview · 28 Nov 2026
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <p class="body case__small">
            <a class="case__inline-link" href={dextra.liveUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Try the live demo ↗</a>
            to see the governance path directly. The screenshot above is the captured dashboard, not a recreation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer class="case__footer">
        <a class="text-link" href={home}>Back to selected work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </article>

  <style>
    .section--case { background: var(--canvas); border-top: 0; }
    .case { max-width: 980px; min-width: 0; }
    .case__head { min-width: 0; margin-bottom: clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px); }
    .case__back {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
      color: var(--secondary);
    }
    .case__back:hover { color: var(--accent); }
    .case__index {
      display: block;
      color: var(--accent);
      margin-top: 20px;
    }
    .case__index::after {
      content: "";
      display: block;
      width: 28px;
      height: 1px;
      margin-top: 8px;
      background: var(--accent);
    }
    .case__eyebrow { margin-top: 14px; }
    .case__title {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
      line-height: 0.92;
      letter-spacing: -0.05em;
      margin-top: 12px;
      overflow-wrap: normal;
      word-break: keep-all;
    }
    .case__subtitle {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
      color: var(--secondary);
      margin-top: 10px;
    }
    .case__lead { margin-top: 24px; max-width: 66ch; }
    .case__strip {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 8px 20px;
      margin-top: 28px;
      padding: 12px 16px;
      background: var(--ink);
      color: var(--white);
      border-radius: 6px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    }
    .case__strip-link { color: var(--white); min-height: 44px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; }
    .case__strip-link:hover { color: var(--secondary-surface); }

    .case__section {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 12px;
      padding-block: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .case__section:first-of-type { border-top: 0; }
    .case__number { font-size: 2rem; color: var(--accent); }
    .case__content { min-width: 0; }
    .case__h2 { margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .case__content .body { max-width: 66ch; color: var(--secondary); }
    .case__small { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 0.9375rem; }

    .case__flow {
      counter-reset: step;
      margin-top: 20px;
      max-width: 66ch;
    }
    .case__flow li {
      counter-increment: step;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 28px minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 12px;
      padding-block: 12px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .case__flow li::before {
      content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--accent);
    }
    .case__flow li .mono { font-weight: 600; }

    .case__tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 20px; }
    .case__tag {
      padding: 5px 10px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 4px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .case__figure { margin: 20px 0 0; min-width: 0; }
    .case__frame {
      aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
      background: var(--secondary-surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .case__frame img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
    .case__figure figcaption { padding-top: 10px; color: var(--secondary); }
    .case__inline-link { color: var(--accent); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent); }

    .case__footer {
      margin-top: clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px);
      padding-top: 24px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    @media (min-width: 768px) {
      .case__section {
        grid-template-columns: 80px minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: 24px;
      }
    }
    @media (max-width: 620px) {
      .case__title { font-size: clamp(3rem, 13vw, 4.25rem); }
      .case__frame { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
      .case__frame img { object-fit: contain; }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .case__section *, .case__frame img { transition: none !important; transform: none !important; }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
